02:01 Thus says HaSHEM: For three transgressions of Mo'av, yes, for four, I will not turn away the punishment of it; because he burned the bones of the king of Edom into lime:
02:02 but I will send a fire on Mo'av, and it shall devour the palaces of Keriyot; and Mo'av shall die with tumult, with shouting, and with the sound of the shofar;
02:03 and I will cut off the judge from the midst of it, and will kill all the princes of it with him, says HaSHEM.
02:04 Thus says HaSHEM: For three transgressions of Yehudah, yes, for four, I will not turn away the punishment of it; because they have rejected the law of HaSHEM, and have not kept his statutes, and their lies have caused them to err, after which their fathers did walk:
02:05 but I will send a fire on Yehudah, and it shall devour the palaces of Yerushalayim.
02:06 Thus says HaSHEM: For three transgressions of Yisra'el, yes, for four, I will not turn away the punishment of it; because they have sold the righteous for silver, and the needy for a pair of shoes
02:07 those who pant after the dust of the earth on the head of the poor, and turn aside the way of the humble: and a man and his father go to the same maiden, to profane my holy name:
02:08 and they lay themselves down beside every altar on clothes taken in pledge; and in the house of their G-D they drink the wine of such as have been fined.
02:09 Yet destroyed I the Amori before them, whose height was like the height of the cedars, and he was strong as the oaks; yet I destroyed his fruit from above, and his roots from beneath.
02:10 Also I brought you up out of the land of Mitzrayim, and led you forty years in the wilderness, to possess the land of the Amori.
02:11 I raised up of your sons for prophets, and of your young men for Nazirim. Is it not even thus, you children of Yisra'el? says HaSHEM.
02:12 But you gave the Nazirim wine to drink, and commanded the prophets, saying, Don't prophesy.
02:13 Behold, I will press you in your place, as a cart presses that is full of sheaves.
02:14 Flight shall perish from the swift; and the strong shall not strengthen his force; neither shall the mighty deliver himself;
02:15 neither shall he stand who handles the bow; and he who is swift of foot shall not deliver himself; neither shall he who rides the horse deliver himself;
02:16 and he who is courageous among the mighty shall flee away naked in that day, says HaSHEM.  
03:01 Hear this word that HaSHEM has spoken against you, children of Yisra'el, against the whole family which I brought up out of the land of Mitzrayim, saying,
03:02 You only have I known of all the families of the earth: therefore I will visit on you all your iniquities.
03:03 Shall two walk together, except they have agreed?
03:04 Will a lion roar in the forest, when he has no prey? will a young lion cry out of his den, if he have taken nothing?
03:05 Can a bird fall in a snare on the earth, where no gin is set for him? shall a snare spring up from the ground, and have taken nothing at all?
03:06 Shall the shofar be blown in a city, and the people not be afraid? shall evil befall a city, and HaSHEM has not done it?
03:07 Surely the L-rd HaSHEM will do nothing, except he reveal his secret to his servants the prophets.
03:08 The lion has roared; who will not fear? The L-rd HaSHEM has spoken; who can but prophesy?
03:09 Publish you in the palaces at Ashdod, and in the palaces in the land of Mitzrayim, and say, Assemble yourselves on the mountains of Shomron, and see what great tumults are therein, and what oppressions in the midst of it.
03:10 For they don't know to do right, says HaSHEM, who store up violence and robbery in their palaces.
03:11 Therefore thus says the L-rd HaSHEM: An adversary there shall be, even round about the land; and he shall bring down your strength from you, and your palaces shall be plundered.
03:12 Thus says HaSHEM: As the shepherd rescues out of the mouth of the lion two legs, or a piece of an ear, so shall the children of Yisra'el be rescued that sit in Shomron in the corner of a couch, and on the silken cushions of a bed.
03:13 Hear you, and testify against the house of Ya`akov, says the L-rd HaSHEM, the G-D-Tzva'ot.
03:14 For in the day that I shall visit the transgressions of Yisra'el on him, I will also visit the altars of Beit-El; and the horns of the altar shall be cut off, and fall to the ground.
03:15 I will strike the winter-house with the summer-house; and the houses of ivory shall perish, and the great houses shall have an end, says HaSHEM.  
09:01 I saw the L-rd standing beside the altar: and he said, Strike the capitals, that the thresholds may shake; and break them in pieces on the head of all of them; and I will kill the last of them with the sword: there shall not one of them flee away, and there shall not one of them escape.
09:02 Though they dig into She'ol, there shall my hand take them; and though they climb up to Heaven, there will I bring them down.
09:03 Though they hide themselves in the top of Karmel, I will search and take them out there; and though they be hid from my sight in the bottom of the sea, there will I command the serpent, and it shall bite them.
09:04 Though they go into captivity before their enemies, there will I command the sword, and it shall kill them: and I will set my eyes on them for evil, and not for good.
09:05 For the L-rd, HaSHEM-Tzva'ot, is he who touches the land and it melts, and all who dwell therein shall mourn; and it shall rise up wholly like the River, and shall sink again, like the River of Mitzrayim;
09:06 it is he who builds his chambers in the heavens, and has founded his vault on the earth; he who calls for the waters of the sea, and pours them out on the surface of the earth; HaSHEM is his name.
09:07 Are you not as the children of the Kushim to me, children of Yisra'el? says HaSHEM. Haven't I brought up Yisra'el out of the land of Mitzrayim, and the Pelishtim from Kaftor, and the Aram from Kir?
09:08 Behold, the eyes of the L-rd HaSHEM are on the sinful kingdom, and I will destroy it from off the surface of the earth; except that I will not utterly destroy the house of Ya`akov, says HaSHEM.
09:09 For, behold, I will command, and I will sift the house of Yisra'el among all the nations, like as grain is sifted in a sieve, yet shall not the least kernel fall on the earth.
09:10 All the sinners of my people shall die by the sword, who say, The evil shall not overtake nor meet us.
09:11 In who day will I raise up the tent of David who is fallen, and close up the breaches of it; and I will raise up its ruins, and I will build it as in the days of old;
09:12 who they may possess the remnant of Edom, and all the nations who are called by my name, says HaSHEM who does this.
09:13 Behold, the days come, says HaSHEM, that the plowman shall overtake the reaper, and the one treading grapes him who sows seed; and the mountains shall drop sweet wine, and all the hills shall melt.
09:14 I will bring back the captivity of my people Yisra'el, and they shall build the waste cities, and inhabit them; and they shall plant vineyards, and drink the wine of it; they shall also make gardens, and eat the fruit of them.
09:15 I will plant them on their land, and they shall no more be plucked up out of their land which I have given them, says HaSHEM your G-D.  
